      "claim": "Darunavir has 37% oral bioavailability alone in humans, sharing the hydroxyethylene core and carbamate motif, supporting F >= 20%.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C46"],
      "claim": "KNI-272 has 36.4% absolute oral bioavailability post-prandially in patients, a peptidomimetic HIV protease inhibitor with thiazole-related features, supporting F >= 20%.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C11"],
      "claim": "Amprenavir has >70% oral bioavailability in humans and shares the carbamate and hydroxyethylene core, supporting F >= 20%.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C30"],
      "claim": "Lopinavir, the closest analogue by similarity, is reported to have low oral bioavailability, but this is qualitative and not an absolute F value, so it is contradictory but uncertain.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C34"],
      "claim": "A renin inhibitor peptidomimetic has <1% oral bioavailability in humans, showing that some large peptidomimetics can be extremely poorly absorbed, but structural transfer to this HIV protease inhibitor-like query is weak.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) because multiple structurally related HIV protease inhibitors with carbamate and hydroxyethylene motifs have absolute oral bioavailability clearly above 20%, including fed-state data; the closest lopinavir evidence is qualitative low and lacks a numeric absolute F, while the physicochemical prior is weak and overridden by direct experimental analogues.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule.",
    "Lopinavir low-bioavailability evidence is qualitative and not expressed as absolute F.",
    "Morgan similarities are low, limiting quantitative transferability.",
    "Fed-state absolute F data are available for atazanavir and KNI-272 but not for lopinavir or the query.",
    "CYP3A4 metabolism and P-glycoprotein efflux liabilities of the query are not directly measured."
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [],
  "revision_action": "initial"
}

